Subject: [PATCH 27/30] artist: support byte accesses and shared image-plane views

Artist has one emulated image-plane store. HP's X11R6.3 NGLE driver clears
it through BINapp0I (0), then uses BINapp1I (1) in SETUP_FB. Map both views to
the existing application RAM block, preserving its migration identity.

Implement the byte-addressed 0x1360 view for byte, halfword and word accesses,
with guest byte order, raster operations and masks. Clip off-screen columns
and rows using the fixed 2048-byte pitch instead of wrapping into other rows.
Ignore writes to unallocated views and bound legacy word reads and dirty
ranges. NEXTSTEP's supported grayscale mode exercises these paths.

Five qtests cover subword preservation, cross-view data, plane/pixel masks,
XOR, edge clipping and unsupported buffer selectors. No new migration state
or Color Recovery implementation is introduced.

Reference: HP NGLE source in X11R6.3, programs/Xserver/hw/hp/ngle/nglehdw.h
(SETUP_FB) and nglescreen.c (ngleDepth8_ClearImagePlanes):
https://www.x.org/releases/X11R6.3/tars/xc-1.tar.gz


